Objective-C messages through selector stubs, as Xcode 27.0's frontend sends them (ADR 0106,
docs/formats/build.md "Swift selector stubs"): on arm64, arm64e and arm64_32 targets, and with
-enable-objc-msgsend-selector-stubs on others (-disable-objc-msgsend-selector-stubs turns them off,
the last of the two wins), a message to an object or a class calls objc_msgSend$<selector>, declared
void (), with an undefined selector argument, and references no selector; messages to super, and the
respondsToSelector: check of an optional or dynamically looked-up method, still go through
objc_msgSend and selector references.

